window.LIFEBOARD_RECIPES=[{"title":"Turkish Menemen with Warm Bread","deck":"Silky eggs folded into jammy tomatoes and sweet green peppers, served straight from the pan.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 12 MIN   |   COOK 22 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Menemen"},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil, or 2 tablespoons oil plus 1 tablespoon butter","name":"extra-virgin olive oil, or 2 tablespoons oil plus 1 tablespoon butter","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3 Turkish sivri peppers or 2 Anaheim peppers, thinly sliced","name":"Turkish sivri peppers or 2 Anaheim peppers, thinly sliced","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 small onion, finely diced (optional; common in home-style versions)","name":"onion, finely diced (optional; common in home-style versions)","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 large ripe tomatoes, peeled and grated, or 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes","name":"ripe tomatoes, peeled and grated, or 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon pul biber or Aleppo pepper, plus more to finish","name":"pul biber or Aleppo pepper, plus more to finish","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"8 large eggs, lightly beaten just until streaky","name":"eggs, lightly beaten just until streaky","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3/4 teaspoon kosher salt, plus freshly ground black pepper","name":"kosher salt, plus freshly ground black pepper","qty":0.75,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons chopped flat-leaf parsley","name":"chopped flat-leaf parsley","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"Warm crusty bread, pide, or simit","name":"Warm crusty bread, pide, or simit","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Extra olive oil and flaky salt","name":"Extra olive oil and flaky salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Heat the oil in a wide skillet over medium heat. Add the peppers and optional onion with a pinch of salt. Cook 8 to 10 minutes, stirring often, until very soft but not browned.","Add the tomatoes and pul biber. Cook uncovered 8 to 12 minutes, until the tomatoes are thick, glossy, and no longer watery. Taste and season before adding the eggs.","Lower the heat to medium-low. Pour in the eggs and fold slowly with a spatula, dragging cooked egg through the tomato mixture while leaving soft curds. Stop while the eggs still look slightly loose; residual heat will finish them.","Finish with black pepper, parsley, a drizzle of olive oil, and more pul biber. Carry the skillet to the table and scoop with warm bread."],"serves":4,"prepMin":12,"cookMin":22,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"The defining texture is spoonable, not dry. Reduce the tomatoes fully first, then cook the eggs gently and pull the pan from the heat early."},{"title":"Shakshuka with Feta and Warm Pita","deck":"North African-inspired eggs poached in a deeply spiced pepper and tomato sauce.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN   |   COOK 35 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Sauce"},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large yellow onion, thinly sliced","name":"yellow onion, thinly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red bell pepper, thinly sliced","name":"red bell pepper, thinly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, thinly sliced","name":"garlic cloves, thinly sliced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon sweet paprika","name":"sweet paprika","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 to 2 tablespoons harissa, to taste","name":"harissa, to taste","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 can (28 ounces) whole peeled tomatoes, crushed by hand","name":"(28 ounces) whole peeled tomatoes, crushed by hand","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":793.8},{"text":"3/4 teaspoon kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":0.75,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Eggs and finish"},{"text":"8 large eggs","name":"eggs","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 ounces feta, crumbled","name":"feta, crumbled","qty":4.0,"unit":"oz","grams":113.4},{"text":"1/3 cup chopped cilantro or parsley","name":"chopped cilantro or parsley","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Warm pita and lemon wedges","name":"Warm pita and lemon wedges","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Heat the olive oil in a large lidded skillet over medium heat. Cook the onion and bell pepper with a pinch of salt for 10 to 12 minutes, until collapsed and lightly caramelized.","Stir in the garlic, cumin, paprika, coriander, and harissa. Cook 45 seconds, then add the tomatoes, salt, and pepper. Simmer 15 to 20 minutes until thick enough to hold a spoon trail.","Make eight wells in the sauce and crack in the eggs. Cover and cook over low heat 5 to 8 minutes, until the whites are set but the yolks remain runny. For firmer yolks, cook 2 minutes longer.","Scatter over the feta and herbs. Finish with a squeeze of lemon and serve immediately with hot pita."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":35,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"A thick sauce is essential. If it is watery before the eggs go in, keep simmering; otherwise the whites become rubbery before the sauce concentrates."},{"title":"French Herb Omelet with Market Vegetables","deck":"A pale, tender omelet with fine herbs and buttery seasonal vegetables folded through the center.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN   |   COOK 20 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Vegetables"},{"text":"1 tablespoon olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 small zucchini, finely diced","name":"zucchini, finely diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cup sliced mushrooms or asparagus pieces","name":"sliced mushrooms or asparagus pieces","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 small shallot, minced","name":"shallot, minced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cup baby spinach","name":"baby spinach","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Kosher salt and black pepper","name":"Kosher salt and black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Omelets"},{"text":"8 large eggs","name":"eggs","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons cold water or heavy cream","name":"cold water or heavy cream","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons chopped chives","name":"chopped chives","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon chopped parsley","name":"chopped parsley","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon chopped tarragon or chervil","name":"chopped tarragon or chervil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"4 tablespoons unsalted butter","name":"unsalted butter","qty":4.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 ounces soft goat cheese or Gruyere, optional","name":"soft goat cheese or Gruyere, optional","qty":2.0,"unit":"oz","grams":56.7}],"steps":["Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Saute the zucchini, mushrooms, and shallot until tender and any moisture has evaporated, 6 to 8 minutes. Fold in the spinach, season, and keep warm.","Whisk the eggs with the water, herbs, 1/2 teaspoon salt, and a few grinds of pepper. Do not whip in excess air.","Make four omelets, using 2 eggs and 1 tablespoon butter for each. Melt the butter over medium-low heat, add the eggs, and stir rapidly with a fork while shaking the pan until tiny soft curds form. Smooth the top while still glossy.","Spoon vegetables and optional cheese down the center. Fold one side inward, roll onto a warm plate seam-side down, and brush with a touch of butter. Serve at once."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":20,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"A classic French omelet should be pale outside and custardy within. Use moderate heat, work quickly, and serve each omelet as soon as it is rolled."},{"title":"Creole Egg and Pepper Scramble","deck":"Fluffy eggs with the Creole trinity, ripe tomato, herbs, and a gentle cayenne kick.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 12 MIN   |   COOK 18 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Scramble"},{"text":"2 tablespoons butter or olive oil","name":"butter or olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/2 green bell pepper, diced","name":"green bell pepper, diced","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 red bell pepper, diced","name":"red bell pepper, diced","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 small onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 celery rib, finely diced","name":"celery rib, finely diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 plum tomato, seeded and diced","name":"plum tomato, seeded and diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Creole seasoning, preferably salt-free","name":"Creole seasoning, preferably salt-free","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon dried thyme","name":"dried thyme","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Pinch of cayenne","name":"Pinch of cayenne","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"8 large eggs","name":"eggs","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons milk or water","name":"milk or water","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 scallions, sliced; hot sauce for serving","name":"scallions, sliced; hot sauce for serving","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"group":"Optional"},{"text":"4 ounces cooked chicken andouille, sliced (use a pork-free brand)","name":"cooked chicken andouille, sliced (use a pork-free brand)","qty":4.0,"unit":"oz","grams":113.4}],"steps":["Melt 1 tablespoon butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add the peppers, onion, celery, and optional chicken andouille. Cook 7 to 9 minutes until tender and lightly browned.","Add the garlic, tomato, Creole seasoning, thyme, and cayenne. Cook 1 to 2 minutes, just until fragrant and the tomato softens.","Whisk the eggs with milk and a pinch of salt. Lower the heat, add the remaining butter, and pour in the eggs. Fold slowly from the edges toward the center until large, moist curds form.","Remove from heat while slightly glossy. Fold in half the scallions and serve with the rest, hot sauce, and toasted bread or grits."],"serves":4,"prepMin":12,"cookMin":18,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"Choose a salt-free Creole blend so you control the seasoning. The vegetables should be fully tender before the eggs enter the pan."},{"title":"Banana Pecan Cinnamon Oats","deck":"Creamy oats layered with caramelized banana, toasted pecans, vanilla, and warm spice.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 5 MIN   |   COOK 15 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Oats"},{"text":"2 cups old-fashioned rolled oats","name":"old-fashioned rolled oats","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups milk or unsweetened oat milk","name":"milk or unsweetened oat milk","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups water","name":"water","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground cinnamon","name":"ground cinnamon","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon vanilla extract","name":"vanilla extract","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Bananas and pecans"},{"text":"3 ripe bananas, sliced","name":"ripe bananas, sliced","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon butter or coconut oil","name":"butter or coconut oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon maple syrup, plus more to serve","name":"maple syrup, plus more to serve","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3/4 cup pecans, roughly chopped and toasted","name":"pecans, roughly chopped and toasted","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Pinch of nutmeg","name":"Pinch of nutmeg","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Bring the milk, water, salt, and cinnamon to a gentle simmer. Stir in the oats and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring often, until creamy. Stir in the vanilla.","Meanwhile, heat the butter in a skillet over medium heat. Arrange two-thirds of the banana slices in one layer and cook 2 minutes per side. Add the maple syrup and nutmeg; toss until glossy.","Mash the remaining banana into the oats for natural sweetness and body. Thin with a splash of milk if needed.","Divide among bowls and top with caramelized banana, toasted pecans, and a small drizzle of maple syrup."],"serves":4,"prepMin":5,"cookMin":15,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"Toasting the pecans and caramelizing the banana makes this taste like banana bread without loading the oats with sugar."},{"title":"Greek Yogurt with Berries, Honey, and Walnuts","deck":"Thick yogurt, bright lemon-macerated berries, floral honey, and warm toasted walnuts.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 10 MIN   |   COOK 5 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Bowls"},{"text":"3 cups full-fat Greek yogurt","name":"full-fat Greek yogurt","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups mixed berries","name":"mixed berries","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon finely grated lemon zest","name":"finely grated lemon zest","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3 to 4 tablespoons good honey","name":"good honey","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3/4 cup walnuts, toasted and roughly chopped","name":"walnuts, toasted and roughly chopped","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon","name":"ground cinnamon","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Pinch of flaky salt","name":"Pinch of flaky salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toss the berries with the lemon zest, lemon juice, and 1 tablespoon honey. Let stand 8 to 10 minutes so their juices begin to run.","Toast the walnuts in a dry skillet over medium-low heat for 4 to 5 minutes, shaking often. Cool briefly and season with a tiny pinch of salt.","Spoon the yogurt into bowls. Top with the berries and their juices, walnuts, remaining honey, and a dusting of cinnamon."],"serves":4,"prepMin":10,"cookMin":5,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"Use true strained Greek yogurt with enough fat for a rich texture. A pinch of salt on the walnuts makes the honey and berries taste brighter."},{"title":"Savory Tofu Scramble with Black Beans","deck":"Crisp-edged tofu, smoky spices, creamy black beans, greens, lime, and fresh cilantro.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 12 MIN   |   COOK 18 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Scramble"},{"text":"1 block (14 to 16 ounces) extra-firm tofu, well drained","name":"(14 to 16 ounces) extra-firm tofu, well drained","qty":1.0,"unit":"block"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/2 onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red bell pepper, diced","name":"red bell pepper, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika","name":"smoked paprika","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon turmeric","name":"turmeric","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons nutritional yeast","name":"nutritional yeast","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 can (15 ounces) black beans, rinsed and drained","name":"(15 ounces) black beans, rinsed and drained","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":425.2},{"text":"2 packed cups baby spinach","name":"baby spinach","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon kala namak, optional, plus kosher salt","name":"kala namak, optional, plus kosher salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 lime and 1/4 cup chopped cilantro","name":"lime and 1/4 cup chopped cilantro","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"}],"steps":["Pat the tofu dry and crumble it into large, irregular pieces. Heat the oil in a wide skillet over medium-high heat and cook the tofu undisturbed for 3 minutes, then toss and brown 3 minutes more.","Add the onion and bell pepper. Cook 5 to 6 minutes until tender. Stir in the garlic, cumin, paprika, turmeric, and nutritional yeast; cook 30 seconds.","Fold in the black beans and spinach with 2 tablespoons water. Cook until the spinach wilts and the beans are hot.","Season with kala namak or kosher salt, black pepper, lime juice, and cilantro. Serve with tortillas, avocado, or roasted potatoes."],"serves":4,"prepMin":12,"cookMin":18,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"Brown the tofu before adding vegetables. That first sear creates the savory texture that many tofu scrambles are missing."},{"title":"Coconut Chia Mango Breakfast Bowl","deck":"Cool coconut chia pudding topped with lime-bright mango and toasted coconut.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 10 MIN + CHILL   |   COOK 3 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chia pudding"},{"text":"1 can (13.5 ounces) full-fat coconut milk","name":"(13.5 ounces) full-fat coconut milk","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":382.7},{"text":"1 cup unsweetened almond milk or water","name":"unsweetened almond milk or water","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup chia seeds","name":"chia seeds","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 tablespoons maple syrup or honey","name":"maple syrup or honey","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon vanilla extract","name":"vanilla extract","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Finely grated zest of 1 lime","name":"Finely grated zest of lime","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Topping"},{"text":"2 ripe mangoes, diced","name":"ripe mangoes, diced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lime juice","name":"lime juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/3 cup unsweetened coconut flakes, toasted","name":"unsweetened coconut flakes, toasted","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Fresh mint, optional","name":"Fresh mint, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Whisk the coconut milk, almond milk, chia seeds, maple syrup, vanilla, lime zest, and salt in a bowl. Rest 10 minutes, whisk again to break up clumps, then cover and refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight.","Toss the mango with lime juice. Toast the coconut in a dry skillet for 2 to 3 minutes until golden.","Stir the pudding and loosen with a splash of milk if very thick. Spoon into bowls and top with mango, toasted coconut, and mint."],"serves":4,"prepMin":10,"cookMin":3,"category":"breakfast","chefNote":"The second whisk after 10 minutes is what prevents dense chia clumps and gives the pudding an even, creamy set."},{"title":"Grilled Chicken Wrap with Lemon Herb Yogurt","deck":"Juicy lemon-oregano chicken, crisp vegetables, and a cool dill yogurt sauce in warm flatbread.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 14 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds boneless skinless chicken thighs","name":"boneless skinless chicken thighs","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Zest and juice of 1 lemon","name":"Zest and juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Lemon herb yogurt"},{"text":"1 cup Greek yogurt","name":"Greek yogurt","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons chopped dill","name":"chopped dill","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons chopped parsley","name":"chopped parsley","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 small garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Pinch of salt","name":"Pinch of salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Wraps"},{"text":"4 large flatbreads or flour tortillas, warmed","name":"flatbreads or flour tortillas, warmed","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Shredded romaine, sliced cucumber, tomato, and red onion","name":"Shredded romaine, sliced cucumber, tomato, and red onion","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toss the chicken with olive oil, lemon zest and juice, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper. Marinate 30 minutes to 4 hours.","Whisk all yogurt sauce ingredients and refrigerate while the chicken marinates.","Grill the chicken over medium-high heat 5 to 7 minutes per side, until deeply marked and 175 F in the thickest part. Rest 5 minutes, then slice across the grain.","Spread each warm flatbread with yogurt sauce. Add vegetables and chicken, tuck in the sides, and roll tightly. Toast seam-side down for 1 minute if desired."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":14,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Chicken thighs stay juicy in a wrap and benefit from reaching about 175 F, where their connective tissue becomes tender."},{"title":"Tijuana-Style Chicken Caesar Salad","deck":"Crisp romaine, grilled chicken, garlicky anchovy dressing, Parmesan, and handmade croutons.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 18 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken and salad"},{"text":"1 1/4 pounds chicken cutlets","name":"chicken cutlets","qty":1.25,"unit":"lb","grams":567.0},{"text":"1 tablespoon olive oil, 1/2 teaspoon salt, and black pepper","name":"olive oil, 1/2 teaspoon salt, and black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3 romaine hearts, leaves separated and thoroughly dried","name":"romaine hearts, leaves separated and thoroughly dried","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 ounces Parmesan, finely grated plus shaved for serving","name":"Parmesan, finely grated plus shaved for serving","qty":2.0,"unit":"oz","grams":56.7},{"group":"Classic-style dressing"},{"text":"2 anchovy fillets, mashed","name":"anchovy fillets, mashed","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 garlic clove, finely grated","name":"garlic clove, finely grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 pasteurized egg yolk or 2 tablespoons mayonnaise","name":"pasteurized egg yolk or 2 tablespoons mayonnaise","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Dijon mustard","name":"Dijon mustard","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce","name":"Worcestershire sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/3 cup extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/4 cup finely grated Parmesan","name":"finely grated Parmesan","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Black pepper","name":"Black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Croutons"},{"text":"3 cups torn day-old bread","name":"torn day-old bread","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Pinch of salt","name":"Pinch of salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toss the bread with oil and salt. Bake at 375 F for 10 to 14 minutes until crisp and golden.","Whisk anchovy, garlic, yolk, Dijon, Worcestershire, and lemon. Slowly whisk in olive oil until glossy, then stir in Parmesan and black pepper. Thin with a teaspoon of water if needed.","Season and grill the chicken over medium-high heat for 4 to 5 minutes per side. Rest, then slice.","Toss the romaine with just enough dressing to coat, then add croutons and grated Parmesan. Plate with chicken and shaved Parmesan. Serve immediately."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":18,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"The original Caesar was created in Tijuana and traditionally had no chicken; this version keeps the punchy tableside-style dressing and adds grilled chicken for lunch."},{"title":"Greek Village Salad with Grilled Chicken","deck":"A proper lettuce-free horiatiki with ripe tomatoes, cucumber, olives, feta, oregano, and lemony chicken.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 12 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"1 1/4 pounds chicken breast or thighs","name":"chicken breast or thighs","qty":1.25,"unit":"lb","grams":567.0},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon red wine vinegar","name":"red wine vinegar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3/4 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.75,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Village salad"},{"text":"4 ripe tomatoes, cut into wedges","name":"ripe tomatoes, cut into wedges","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 English cucumber, thickly sliced","name":"English cucumber, thickly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 green bell pepper, thinly sliced","name":"green bell pepper, thinly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 red onion, thinly sliced","name":"red onion, thinly sliced","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3/4 cup Kalamata olives","name":"Kalamata olives","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"6 ounces feta in one slab or large pieces","name":"feta in one slab or large pieces","qty":6.0,"unit":"oz","grams":170.1},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon red wine vinegar","name":"red wine vinegar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried Greek oregano","name":"dried Greek oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Salt and black pepper","name":"Salt and black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Marinate the chicken with olive oil, vinegar, oregano, garlic, and salt for 20 minutes or up to 4 hours.","Grill over medium-high heat until cooked through, 5 to 7 minutes per side depending on thickness. Rest and slice.","Combine tomatoes, cucumber, pepper, onion, and olives. Season lightly with salt, then dress with olive oil, vinegar, oregano, and pepper.","Lay the feta in large pieces over the salad, drizzle with a little more olive oil, and serve the chicken alongside."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":12,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Salt the salad only just before serving, and keep the feta in substantial pieces. Greek village salad is juicy and rustic, never a bowl of lettuce."},{"title":"Chicken Souvlaki Pita with Tzatziki","deck":"Lemon-garlic chicken skewers tucked into hot pita with tomato, onion, and cool cucumber yogurt.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 12 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Souvlaki"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds boneless skinless chicken thighs, cut in 1 1/2-inch pieces","name":"boneless skinless chicken thighs, cut in 1 1/2-inch pieces","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Juice of 1 lemon","name":"Juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Tzatziki"},{"text":"1 cup Greek yogurt","name":"Greek yogurt","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 English cucumber, grated and squeezed dry","name":"English cucumber, grated and squeezed dry","qty":0.5,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons chopped dill","name":"chopped dill","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Salt to taste","name":"Salt to taste","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"4 pita breads, warmed","name":"pita breads, warmed","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Sliced tomato and red onion","name":"Sliced tomato and red onion","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Chopped parsley","name":"Chopped parsley","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Marinate the chicken with olive oil, lemon, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper for at least 30 minutes and no more than 6 hours.","Mix the tzatziki ingredients and chill. Squeezing the cucumber very dry keeps the sauce thick.","Thread the chicken onto skewers. Grill over high heat 8 to 12 minutes, turning several times, until charred at the edges and cooked through.","Brush warm pita lightly with olive oil. Fill with chicken, tomato, onion, parsley, and generous tzatziki."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":12,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Do not marinate chicken overnight in lemon; prolonged acid exposure makes the surface mealy. Thirty minutes to six hours is ideal."},{"title":"Grilled Cheese with Roasted Tomato Soup","deck":"Deeply roasted tomato soup paired with a crisp sourdough sandwich and molten cheddar-Gruyere center.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN   |   COOK 50 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Soup"},{"text":"2 pounds ripe tomatoes, halved, plus 1 can (14 ounces) tomatoes if needed","name":"ripe tomatoes, halved, plus 1 can (14 ounces) tomatoes if needed","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":396.9},{"text":"1 yellow onion, cut in wedges","name":"yellow onion, cut in wedges","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"6 garlic cloves, unpeeled","name":"garlic cloves, unpeeled","qty":6.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 cups vegetable or chicken stock","name":"vegetable or chicken stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon dried thyme","name":"dried thyme","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 cup basil leaves","name":"basil leaves","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/3 cup heavy cream, optional","name":"heavy cream, optional","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"group":"Sandwiches"},{"text":"8 slices sourdough bread","name":"sourdough bread","qty":8.0,"unit":"slice"},{"text":"6 ounces sharp cheddar, grated","name":"sharp cheddar, grated","qty":6.0,"unit":"oz","grams":170.1},{"text":"4 ounces Gruyere, grated","name":"Gruyere, grated","qty":4.0,"unit":"oz","grams":113.4},{"text":"3 tablespoons softened butter or mayonnaise","name":"softened butter or mayonnaise","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"}],"steps":["Roast tomatoes, onion, and garlic with olive oil, salt, and pepper at 425 F for 30 to 35 minutes, until the edges caramelize. Squeeze the garlic from its skins.","Transfer to a pot with stock and thyme. Simmer 10 minutes, add basil, then blend until smooth. Stir in cream if using and adjust salt and acidity with a small splash of vinegar if needed.","Combine the cheeses. Build four sandwiches, spreading the outsides of the bread with butter or mayonnaise.","Cook in a covered skillet over medium-low heat 3 to 4 minutes per side, pressing gently, until deeply golden and fully melted. Serve with hot soup."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":50,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Grate the cheese and cook over medium-low heat. High heat browns the bread before the center has time to melt."},{"title":"Chinese-American Chicken and Broccoli Bowl","deck":"Velvety chicken, crisp-tender broccoli, and glossy brown sauce over steamed rice.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 15 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"1 1/4 pounds chicken breast, thinly sliced across the grain","name":"chicken breast, thinly sliced across the grain","qty":1.25,"unit":"lb","grams":567.0},{"text":"1 tablespoon light soy sauce","name":"light soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon Shaoxing wine or dry sherry","name":"Shaoxing wine or dry sherry","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Sauce"},{"text":"3/4 cup low-sodium chicken stock","name":"low-sodium chicken stock","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 tablespoons light soy sauce","name":"light soy sauce","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dark soy sauce, optional","name":"dark soy sauce, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon Shaoxing wine","name":"Shaoxing wine","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon toasted sesame oil","name":"toasted sesame oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon sugar","name":"sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 tablespoons cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":1.5,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Black or white pepper","name":"Black or white pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Stir-fry"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds broccoli florets","name":"broccoli florets","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"2 tablespoons neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"4 cups cooked jasmine rice","name":"cooked jasmine rice","qty":4.0,"unit":"cup"}],"steps":["Mix the chicken with soy, wine, cornstarch, and oil; rest 15 minutes. Whisk all sauce ingredients in a separate bowl.","Blanch broccoli in salted boiling water for 60 to 90 seconds. Drain very well.","Heat a wok or large skillet until very hot. Add 1 tablespoon oil and sear chicken in one layer, working in batches if needed, until nearly cooked. Transfer out.","Add remaining oil, garlic, and ginger for 15 seconds. Add broccoli, chicken, and sauce. Toss 1 to 2 minutes until glossy and thickened. Serve over rice."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":15,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"This sauce is shellfish-free and does not require oyster sauce. Velveting with cornstarch protects the lean chicken from drying out."},{"title":"Greek Roasted Vegetable and Chickpea Bowl","deck":"Oregano-roasted vegetables and chickpeas over lemon-dill rice with feta and a bright yogurt drizzle.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 18 MIN   |   COOK 38 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Roast"},{"text":"1 small eggplant, diced","name":"eggplant, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 zucchini, diced","name":"zucchini, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red bell pepper, diced","name":"red bell pepper, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red onion, cut in wedges","name":"red onion, cut in wedges","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 can (15 ounces) chickpeas, drained and dried","name":"(15 ounces) chickpeas, drained and dried","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":425.2},{"text":"3 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Rice and finish"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups long-grain rice, rinsed","name":"long-grain rice, rinsed","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 1/4 cups vegetable stock","name":"vegetable stock","qty":2.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Zest and juice of 1 lemon","name":"Zest and juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/4 cup chopped dill","name":"chopped dill","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"4 ounces feta, crumbled","name":"feta, crumbled","qty":4.0,"unit":"oz","grams":113.4},{"text":"1 cup Greek yogurt thinned with 1 tablespoon water","name":"Greek yogurt thinned with 1 tablespoon water","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Cucumber, olives, and parsley","name":"Cucumber, olives, and parsley","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Heat the oven to 425 F. Toss eggplant, zucchini, pepper, onion, and chickpeas with olive oil, oregano, cumin, and salt. Roast 28 to 35 minutes, turning once, until browned.","Meanwhile, simmer the rice in stock, covered, for 15 minutes. Rest off heat 10 minutes, then fluff with lemon zest, half the lemon juice, and dill.","Season the yogurt with the remaining lemon juice and a pinch of salt.","Build bowls with lemon rice, roasted vegetables and chickpeas, cucumber, olives, feta, parsley, and yogurt sauce."],"serves":4,"prepMin":18,"cookMin":38,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Dry the chickpeas and give the vegetables room on the pan. Crowding traps steam and prevents the browned edges that make the bowl satisfying."},{"title":"Lebanese-Style Mujadara with Tomato Cucumber Salad","deck":"Earthy lentils and rice crowned with deeply caramelized onions, served with a crisp lemony salad.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 55 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Mujadara"},{"text":"1 cup brown or green lentils, rinsed","name":"brown or green lentils, rinsed","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3/4 cup long-grain rice, rinsed","name":"long-grain rice, rinsed","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"4 large yellow onions, thinly sliced","name":"yellow onions, thinly sliced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 cup olive oil, divided","name":"olive oil, divided","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground allspice","name":"ground allspice","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"4 1/2 cups water, divided","name":"water, divided","qty":4.5,"unit":"cup"},{"group":"Salad"},{"text":"3 tomatoes, diced","name":"tomatoes, diced","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 English cucumber, diced","name":"English cucumber, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/4 red onion, finely diced","name":"red onion, finely diced","qty":0.25,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/3 cup chopped parsley","name":"chopped parsley","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice of 1 lemon","name":"Juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Salt and pepper","name":"Salt and pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cook the onions in 6 tablespoons olive oil over medium heat with a pinch of salt, stirring often, for 30 to 40 minutes. They should become dark mahogany, sweet, and crisp at the edges. Reserve half for topping.","Meanwhile, simmer lentils in 3 cups water for 15 minutes. Add rice, cumin, allspice, salt, remaining water, and the softer half of the onions. Cover and simmer 15 minutes, then rest 10 minutes off heat.","Toss all salad ingredients and season brightly with lemon and salt.","Fluff the mujadara, spoon onto a platter, and cover with the reserved onions. Serve warm or room temperature with salad and yogurt if desired."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":55,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"The onions are the soul of mujadara. Take them past golden into deep brown without burning; their sweetness seasons the entire pot."},{"title":"Thai-Style Peanut Tofu Vegetable Bowl","deck":"Crisp tofu and colorful vegetables with a creamy lime-peanut sauce over jasmine rice.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 22 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Bowl"},{"text":"1 block (14 ounces) extra-firm tofu, pressed and cubed","name":"(14 ounces) extra-firm tofu, pressed and cubed","qty":1.0,"unit":"block","grams":396.9},{"text":"1 tablespoon cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 red bell pepper, sliced","name":"red bell pepper, sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 cups broccoli florets","name":"broccoli florets","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 cup snap peas or green beans","name":"snap peas or green beans","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"4 cups cooked jasmine rice","name":"cooked jasmine rice","qty":4.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Thai basil or cilantro, lime wedges, and chopped peanuts","name":"Thai basil or cilantro, lime wedges, and chopped peanuts","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Peanut sauce"},{"text":"1/2 cup smooth peanut butter","name":"smooth peanut butter","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/3 cup coconut milk or hot water","name":"coconut milk or hot water","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 tablespoons lime juice","name":"lime juice","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 tablespoons soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":1.5,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon brown sugar","name":"brown sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 small garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 to 2 teaspoons sambal oelek or chili-garlic sauce","name":"sambal oelek or chili-garlic sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"}],"steps":["Toss the tofu with cornstarch and a pinch of salt. Sear in 1 tablespoon oil over medium-high heat until crisp on several sides, 8 to 10 minutes. Transfer out.","Whisk the peanut sauce until smooth, adding enough coconut milk or water for a pourable consistency.","Add remaining oil to the pan and stir-fry the pepper, broccoli, and snap peas for 5 to 7 minutes, leaving them crisp-tender. Return tofu and add half the sauce; toss until hot.","Serve over rice with extra sauce, herbs, lime, and peanuts."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":22,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"This is a modern Thai-inspired bowl rather than a canonical Thai dish. The balance should be salty, sour, sweet, spicy, and nutty - adjust with soy, lime, sugar, and chile."},{"title":"Mediterranean Chickpea Tahini Wrap","deck":"Warm cumin-spiced chickpeas, crunchy vegetables, herbs, and lemon tahini rolled in soft flatbread.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 18 MIN   |   COOK 10 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chickpeas"},{"text":"2 cans (15 ounces each) chickpeas, rinsed and drained","name":"(15 ounces each) chickpeas, rinsed and drained","qty":2.0,"unit":"can"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika","name":"smoked paprika","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Lemon tahini"},{"text":"1/2 cup tahini","name":"tahini","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/3 cup cold water, plus more as needed","name":"cold water, plus more as needed","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice of 1 lemon","name":"Juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon salt","name":"salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Wraps"},{"text":"4 large flatbreads","name":"flatbreads","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Shredded lettuce or cabbage","name":"Shredded lettuce or cabbage","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Diced tomato and cucumber","name":"Diced tomato and cucumber","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Quick-pickled red onion","name":"Quick-pickled red onion","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Parsley and mint","name":"Parsley and mint","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cook chickpeas in olive oil with cumin, coriander, paprika, and salt over medium-high heat for 8 to 10 minutes, until hot and lightly crisp. Crush a few with the back of a spoon.","Whisk tahini and lemon; it will tighten. Gradually whisk in cold water until pale, smooth, and pourable. Stir in garlic and salt.","Warm the flatbreads. Layer with cabbage, tomato, cucumber, chickpeas, pickled onion, herbs, and tahini.","Fold the bottom upward, tuck in the sides, and roll. Toast seam-side down briefly for a crisp exterior."],"serves":4,"prepMin":18,"cookMin":10,"category":"lunch","chefNote":"Cold water transforms tahini from stiff to creamy. Add it gradually and keep whisking through the moment the sauce seizes."},{"title":"Charcoal-Style Grilled Chicken with Seasonal Vegetables","deck":"Smoky, lemon-garlic chicken with blistered vegetables and a fresh herb finish.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 35 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"3 pounds bone-in chicken thighs and drumsticks","name":"bone-in chicken thighs and drumsticks","qty":3.0,"unit":"lb","grams":1360.8},{"text":"1/3 cup extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice and zest of 2 lemons","name":"Juice and zest of lemons","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"5 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":5.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon smoked paprika","name":"smoked paprika","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Vegetables"},{"text":"2 zucchini, cut lengthwise","name":"zucchini, cut lengthwise","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 bell peppers, quartered","name":"bell peppers, quartered","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red onion, cut in thick rounds","name":"red onion, cut in thick rounds","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 pint cherry tomatoes","name":"pint cherry tomatoes","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil and salt","name":"olive oil and salt","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Parsley, mint, and lemon wedges","name":"Parsley, mint, and lemon wedges","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Marinate the chicken with olive oil, lemon, garlic, oregano, paprika, salt, and pepper for 2 to 8 hours.","Prepare a two-zone charcoal grill. Brown the chicken skin-side down over direct medium heat, turning as needed, 8 to 10 minutes. Move to the cooler side, cover, and cook until the thighs reach 175 F, 20 to 25 minutes more.","Toss the vegetables with olive oil and salt. Grill over direct heat until deeply marked and tender, 3 to 6 minutes per side. Skewer or pan-grill the tomatoes until blistered.","Rest the chicken 8 minutes. Finish everything with chopped herbs, lemon, and a drizzle of good olive oil."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":35,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"A two-zone fire gives you char without burned skin. Bone-in dark meat is best at 175 F, not merely 165 F, because the extra heat tenderizes it."},{"title":"Herb-Baked Chicken with Root Vegetables","deck":"Crisp-skinned chicken roasted over caramelized roots with rosemary, thyme, garlic, and pan juices.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 55 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Roast"},{"text":"6 bone-in skin-on chicken thighs","name":"bone-in skin-on chicken thighs","qty":6.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 pound carrots, cut in large pieces","name":"carrots, cut in large pieces","qty":1.0,"unit":"lb","grams":453.6},{"text":"2 parsnips, cut in large pieces","name":"parsnips, cut in large pieces","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 large sweet potato, cubed","name":"sweet potato, cubed","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red onion, cut in wedges","name":"red onion, cut in wedges","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"8 garlic cloves, lightly crushed","name":"garlic cloves, lightly crushed","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon chopped rosemary","name":"chopped rosemary","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon thyme leaves","name":"thyme leaves","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon lemon zest","name":"lemon zest","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt and 3/4 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 3/4 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 cup chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"}],"steps":["Heat the oven to 425 F. Pat the chicken very dry. Toss the vegetables and garlic with 2 tablespoons oil, half the herbs, 3/4 teaspoon salt, and pepper in a large roasting pan.","Rub chicken with remaining oil, herbs, lemon zest, salt, and pepper. Arrange skin-side up over the vegetables and pour stock around, not over, the chicken.","Roast 45 to 55 minutes, stirring the vegetables once, until the skin is crisp and the thighs reach 175 F.","Transfer chicken to a plate. Toss vegetables with lemon juice and scrape up the browned pan juices. Rest chicken 8 minutes before serving."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":55,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Keeping the stock below the chicken preserves crisp skin while the drippings season the vegetables."},{"title":"Buttermilk Fried Chicken with Braised Greens","deck":"Craggy, deeply seasoned fried chicken with tender collards braised in smoky turkey broth.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN + BRINE   |   COOK 75 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken brine"},{"text":"3 pounds bone-in chicken pieces","name":"bone-in chicken pieces","qty":3.0,"unit":"lb","grams":1360.8},{"text":"2 cups buttermilk","name":"buttermilk","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 tablespoons hot sauce","name":"hot sauce","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon garlic powder","name":"garlic powder","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Dredge and frying"},{"text":"2 cups all-purpose flour","name":"all-purpose flour","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 teaspoons paprika","name":"paprika","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon onion powder","name":"onion powder","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon garlic powder","name":"garlic powder","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon cayenne","name":"cayenne","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 teaspoons kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Peanut or canola oil, for frying","name":"Peanut or canola oil, for frying","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Braised greens"},{"text":"2 pounds collard greens, stems removed and leaves sliced","name":"collard greens, stems removed and leaves sliced","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"1 smoked turkey wing or 6 ounces smoked turkey, optional","name":"smoked turkey wing or 6 ounces smoked turkey, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 garlic cloves, sliced","name":"garlic cloves, sliced","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 cups chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":4.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon apple cider vinegar","name":"apple cider vinegar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Pinch of red pepper flakes","name":"Pinch of red pepper flakes","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Marinate chicken in buttermilk, hot sauce, salt, pepper, and garlic powder for 8 to 24 hours.","For the greens, cook onion and garlic in a little oil until soft. Add turkey, stock, red pepper, and greens. Cover and simmer 45 to 60 minutes until tender. Finish with vinegar and salt.","Combine dredge ingredients. Drizzle in 3 tablespoons of the buttermilk marinade and rub with your fingers to form small clumps. Lift chicken from marinade, let excess drip, then press firmly into the dredge. Rest on a rack 15 minutes.","Heat 2 inches oil to 325 F in a heavy pot. Fry in batches without crowding, turning every few minutes, until mahogany brown and the breast reaches 165 F or dark meat 175 F, about 12 to 18 minutes.","Drain on a rack, not paper towels. Season lightly while hot and rest 8 minutes before serving with greens."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":75,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"The clumpy dredge creates the craggy crust. Keep the oil near 325 F and use a thermometer; temperature control is the difference between crisp and greasy."},{"title":"Chicken Parmesan with Spaghetti","deck":"Crisp Parmesan-panko cutlets, bright marinara, bubbling mozzarella, and properly sauced spaghetti.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 35 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"4 chicken cutlets, about 6 ounces each","name":"chicken cutlets, about 6 ounces each","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 cup flour","name":"flour","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 large eggs, beaten","name":"eggs, beaten","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cup panko breadcrumbs","name":"panko breadcrumbs","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup finely grated Parmesan","name":"finely grated Parmesan","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Kosher salt and black pepper","name":"Kosher salt and black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Olive or neutral oil, for shallow frying","name":"Olive or neutral oil, for shallow frying","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Sauce and pasta"},{"text":"3 cups good marinara sauce","name":"good marinara sauce","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"8 ounces low-moisture mozzarella, grated","name":"low-moisture mozzarella, grated","qty":8.0,"unit":"oz","grams":226.8},{"text":"2 ounces provolone, grated, optional","name":"provolone, grated, optional","qty":2.0,"unit":"oz","grams":56.7},{"text":"12 ounces spaghetti","name":"spaghetti","qty":12.0,"unit":"oz","grams":340.2},{"text":"Basil leaves and extra Parmesan","name":"Basil leaves and extra Parmesan","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Season chicken well. Set up flour, eggs, and panko mixed with Parmesan and oregano. Coat each cutlet in flour, egg, then crumbs, pressing firmly. Rest 10 minutes.","Heat 1/4 inch oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Fry cutlets 3 to 4 minutes per side until crisp and just cooked. Drain on a rack.","Spread a thin layer of marinara in a baking dish. Add chicken, spoon only 2 to 3 tablespoons sauce over each so the crust remains crisp, and top with mozzarella and provolone. Broil until bubbling and spotted brown.","Boil spaghetti in well-salted water until al dente. Toss with enough hot marinara to coat and a splash of pasta water. Serve beside the chicken with basil and Parmesan."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":35,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Sauce the cutlet lightly and serve extra sauce with the pasta. Drowning the breading before broiling erases the crisp texture you worked to create."},{"title":"Chinese-American Chicken and Broccoli","deck":"A restaurant-style wok dinner with tender dark-meat chicken, vibrant broccoli, and savory garlic sauce.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 22 MIN   |   COOK 16 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds boneless skinless chicken thighs, thinly sliced","name":"boneless skinless chicken thighs, thinly sliced","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"1 tablespoon soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon Shaoxing wine","name":"Shaoxing wine","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon baking soda","name":"baking soda","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Sauce"},{"text":"1 cup chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 1/2 tablespoons soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":2.5,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dark soy sauce","name":"dark soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon Shaoxing wine","name":"Shaoxing wine","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon sugar","name":"sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon toasted sesame oil","name":"toasted sesame oil","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 tablespoons cornstarch","name":"cornstarch","qty":1.5,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"White pepper","name":"White pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Stir-fry"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds broccoli florets","name":"broccoli florets","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"2 tablespoons neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Steamed rice","name":"Steamed rice","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Mix chicken with marinade ingredients and rest 20 minutes. Whisk sauce separately. Blanch broccoli in salted water for 75 seconds and drain thoroughly.","Heat a wok until faintly smoking. Add 1 tablespoon oil, spread chicken in one layer, and sear 60 seconds before tossing. Cook until about 80 percent done, then transfer out.","Add remaining oil, garlic, and ginger. Stir 10 seconds, add broccoli and chicken, then pour in the re-whisked sauce.","Toss over high heat until the sauce boils, turns glossy, and clings to the food, 1 to 2 minutes. Serve immediately with rice."],"serves":4,"prepMin":22,"cookMin":16,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Baking soda is used in a very small amount to tenderize dark meat. Do not increase it, and do not marinate longer than 30 minutes."},{"title":"Tokyo-Style Shoyu Ramen with Egg","deck":"Clear chicken-dashi broth, soy tare, scallion aroma oil, springy noodles, chicken, and marinated eggs.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 35 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 3 HR","ingredients":[{"group":"Chicken broth"},{"text":"3 pounds chicken wings and backs","name":"chicken wings and backs","qty":3.0,"unit":"lb","grams":1360.8},{"text":"12 cups cold water","name":"cold water","qty":12.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 onion, halved","name":"onion, halved","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 head garlic, halved crosswise","name":"head garlic, halved crosswise","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2-inch piece ginger, sliced","name":"2-inch piece ginger, sliced","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"4 scallions","name":"scallions","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"group":"Dashi and tare"},{"text":"1 piece kombu, about 4 by 4 inches","name":"piece kombu, about 4 by 4 inches","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 dried shiitake mushrooms","name":"dried shiitake mushrooms","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 cups water","name":"water","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 packed cup katsuobushi, optional but traditional","name":"katsuobushi, optional but traditional","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup Japanese soy sauce","name":"Japanese soy sauce","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/4 cup mirin","name":"mirin","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/4 cup sake","name":"sake","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon sugar","name":"sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon fine sea salt","name":"fine sea salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Eggs, oil, and bowls"},{"text":"4 large eggs","name":"eggs","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/4 cup soy sauce, 1/4 cup mirin, and 1/2 cup water for soaking","name":"soy sauce, 1/4 cup mirin, and 1/2 cup water for soaking","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3 tablespoons chicken fat or neutral oil","name":"chicken fat or neutral oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 scallions, chopped; 3 slices ginger","name":"scallions, chopped; 3 slices ginger","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 portions fresh ramen noodles","name":"portions fresh ramen noodles","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 cooked chicken thighs, sliced","name":"cooked chicken thighs, sliced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Nori, menma, scallions, and spinach, as desired","name":"Nori, menma, scallions, and spinach, as desired","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["For the broth, cover chicken with cold water and bring slowly to a bare simmer. Skim thoroughly. Add onion, garlic, ginger, and scallions; simmer uncovered 2 1/2 hours without a hard boil. Strain and keep hot.","For dashi, soak kombu and shiitake in 2 cups water for 30 minutes. Heat until steaming but not boiling; remove kombu. Simmer shiitake 5 minutes, turn off heat, add katsuobushi, steep 5 minutes, and strain. Combine dashi with chicken broth.","For tare, simmer soy, mirin, sake, sugar, and salt for 3 minutes; cool. For aroma oil, gently fry chopped scallion and ginger in chicken fat or oil for 8 minutes, then strain.","For ajitama, boil eggs 6 1/2 minutes, chill in ice water, peel, and soak in the soy-mirin-water mixture 4 to 12 hours. Halve before serving.","Cook noodles according to package directions and drain very well. In each warmed bowl place 2 tablespoons tare and 1 teaspoon aroma oil. Add 1 1/2 to 2 cups boiling broth, taste, and adjust with a little more tare.","Add noodles immediately. Top with chicken, egg, nori, menma, scallions, and spinach. Serve at once."],"serves":4,"prepMin":35,"cookMin":0,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Ramen is assembled from separate seasoned components. Taste one test bowl before serving all four; the correct amount of tare depends on the saltiness of your soy sauce and broth."},{"title":"Vietnamese Chicken Pho","deck":"Clear, aromatic chicken broth with charred onion and ginger, toasted spices, rice noodles, and fresh herbs.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 90 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Broth"},{"text":"1 whole chicken, 4 to 4 1/2 pounds","name":"whole chicken, 4 to 4 1/2 pounds","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"12 cups water","name":"water","qty":12.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 large onion, halved","name":"onion, halved","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4-inch piece ginger, halved lengthwise","name":"4-inch piece ginger, halved lengthwise","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"2 star anise","name":"star anise","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cinnamon stick","name":"cinnamon stick","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon coriander seeds","name":"coriander seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon fennel seeds","name":"fennel seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"4 cloves","name":"","qty":4.0,"unit":"clove"},{"text":"1 black cardamom pod, optional","name":"black cardamom pod, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons fish sauce","name":"fish sauce","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon rock sugar or light brown sugar","name":"rock sugar or light brown sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Bowls"},{"text":"12 ounces flat rice noodles","name":"flat rice noodles","qty":12.0,"unit":"oz","grams":340.2},{"text":"Thinly sliced onion and scallions","name":"Thinly sliced onion and scallions","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Cilantro, Thai basil, bean sprouts, lime, and fresh chiles","name":"Cilantro, Thai basil, bean sprouts, lime, and fresh chiles","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Hoisin and sriracha, optional at the table","name":"Hoisin and sriracha, optional at the table","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Char the onion and ginger cut-side down under a broiler or in a dry skillet until blackened in spots. Rinse away loose soot. Toast whole spices in a dry pan for 2 minutes and tie in cheesecloth.","Place chicken in a stockpot with water. Bring to a gentle simmer and skim. Add charred aromatics and spice bundle. Simmer very gently 40 to 50 minutes, until the chicken is cooked.","Remove chicken to cool. Continue simmering broth 20 minutes. Strain, then season with fish sauce, sugar, and salt. The broth should taste slightly stronger than a soup because noodles will dilute it.","Pull chicken meat into bite-size pieces. Soak or cook noodles according to package directions and drain.","Divide noodles and chicken among warm bowls. Ladle over boiling broth and top with onion and scallion. Serve herbs, sprouts, lime, and chiles alongside."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":90,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Never let pho broth boil aggressively. A bare simmer and frequent skimming preserve the clear, clean flavor."},{"title":"Texas Red Beef Chili","deck":"Tender beef in a brick-red dried-chile gravy with cumin, garlic, oregano, and no beans.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 3 HR","ingredients":[{"group":"Chile paste"},{"text":"4 dried ancho chiles, stemmed and seeded","name":"dried ancho chiles, stemmed and seeded","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 dried guajillo chiles, stemmed and seeded","name":"dried guajillo chiles, stemmed and seeded","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 dried pasilla chiles, stemmed and seeded","name":"dried pasilla chiles, stemmed and seeded","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 cups hot beef stock","name":"hot beef stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"group":"Chili"},{"text":"3 pounds beef chuck, cut in 1 1/2-inch cubes","name":"beef chuck, cut in 1 1/2-inch cubes","qty":3.0,"unit":"lb","grams":1360.8},{"text":"2 teaspoons kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"3 tablespoons neutral oil or beef tallow","name":"neutral oil or beef tallow","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"5 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":5.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Mexican oregano","name":"Mexican oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons tomato paste, optional","name":"tomato paste, optional","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 to 3 cups beef stock","name":"beef stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon masa harina mixed with 2 tablespoons water, optional","name":"masa harina mixed with 2 tablespoons water, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Apple cider vinegar and salt to finish","name":"Apple cider vinegar and salt to finish","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toast dried chiles in a dry skillet for 15 to 20 seconds per side. Cover with hot stock for 20 minutes, then blend completely smooth.","Season beef. Brown in batches in hot oil, building a dark crust without crowding. Transfer to a bowl.","Cook onion until golden, 8 minutes. Add garlic, cumin, oregano, coriander, and optional tomato paste; cook 1 minute. Stir in chile puree and simmer 5 minutes.","Return beef and add enough stock to barely cover. Simmer partially covered 2 1/2 to 3 hours until fork-tender, stirring occasionally. Add water if it becomes too thick before the beef softens.","For a thicker gravy, stir in masa slurry and simmer 10 minutes. Finish with a teaspoon or two of vinegar and adjust salt."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":0,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"True Texas red centers beef and dried chiles, not beans. Toast the chiles briefly; burned chiles make the entire pot bitter."},{"title":"Greek Lamb Souvlaki with Lemon Potatoes","deck":"Charred oregano-lemon lamb skewers with potatoes roasted in garlicky broth until crisp and creamy.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 70 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Lamb souvlaki"},{"text":"2 pounds boneless leg of lamb, cut in 1 1/2-inch cubes","name":"boneless leg of lamb, cut in 1 1/2-inch cubes","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"1/4 cup extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice and zest of 1 lemon","name":"Juice and zest of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Lemon potatoes"},{"text":"2 pounds Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in wedges","name":"Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in wedges","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"1/3 cup olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice of 2 lemons","name":"Juice of lemons","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Dijon mustard","name":"Dijon mustard","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Salt and black pepper","name":"Salt and black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"Tzatziki, parsley, red onion, and lemon wedges","name":"Tzatziki, parsley, red onion, and lemon wedges","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Marinate lamb with olive oil, lemon, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper for 2 to 8 hours.","Heat oven to 425 F. Toss potatoes with all remaining potato ingredients in a roasting pan. Roast 45 minutes, turn, then continue 20 to 25 minutes until the stock is absorbed and the edges are crisp.","Thread lamb onto skewers. Grill over high heat 8 to 10 minutes, turning, for medium-rare to medium. Rest 5 minutes.","Serve skewers with lemon potatoes, tzatziki, parsley, onion, and fresh lemon."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":70,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Boneless leg gives clean cubes and a rosy center. If using shoulder, cook it a little longer to medium so its connective tissue softens."},{"title":"Greek Lemon Lamb with Roasted Vegetables","deck":"Slow-roasted lamb shoulder perfumed with lemon, garlic, oregano, rosemary, and white wine.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 3 HR 30 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Lamb and vegetables"},{"text":"1 boneless lamb shoulder, 3 1/2 to 4 pounds","name":"boneless lamb shoulder, 3 1/2 to 4 pounds","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/4 cup olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Juice and zest of 2 lemons","name":"Juice and zest of lemons","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"8 garlic cloves, sliced","name":"garlic cloves, sliced","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon chopped rosemary","name":"chopped rosemary","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 cup dry white wine or chicken stock","name":"dry white wine or chicken stock","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 large eggplant, cut in chunks","name":"eggplant, cut in chunks","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 zucchini, cut in chunks","name":"zucchini, cut in chunks","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 bell peppers, cut in chunks","name":"bell peppers, cut in chunks","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 red onion, cut in wedges","name":"red onion, cut in wedges","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 pint cherry tomatoes","name":"pint cherry tomatoes","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"}],"steps":["Heat oven to 325 F. Season lamb all over. Mix olive oil, lemon zest and juice, garlic, oregano, and rosemary; rub over lamb.","Place lamb in a covered roasting pan with wine. Roast 2 1/2 hours, turning once, until beginning to soften.","Raise oven to 400 F. Arrange eggplant, zucchini, peppers, onion, and tomatoes around the lamb; season and toss in the pan juices. Roast uncovered 45 to 60 minutes until lamb is pull-apart tender and vegetables are browned.","Rest lamb 20 minutes. Skim excess fat from the juices, squeeze in more lemon if needed, and spoon over sliced or pulled lamb and vegetables."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":0,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Lamb shoulder rewards patience. It is ready when a fork twists easily, not simply when it reaches a particular internal temperature."},{"title":"Greek Briam Roasted Vegetables with Feta","deck":"A lavish pan of eggplant, zucchini, potato, tomato, onion, herbs, and olive oil roasted until jammy.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 80 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Briam"},{"text":"1 medium eggplant, sliced 1/3 inch thick","name":"eggplant, sliced 1/3 inch thick","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 zucchini, sliced 1/3 inch thick","name":"zucchini, sliced 1/3 inch thick","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds Yukon Gold potatoes, thinly sliced","name":"Yukon Gold potatoes, thinly sliced","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"1 large onion, thinly sliced","name":"onion, thinly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 ripe tomatoes, grated or thinly sliced","name":"ripe tomatoes, grated or thinly sliced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, thinly sliced","name":"garlic cloves, thinly sliced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 cup extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup chopped parsley","name":"chopped parsley","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 cup water","name":"water","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"6 ounces feta, for serving","name":"feta, for serving","qty":6.0,"unit":"oz","grams":170.1}],"steps":["Heat oven to 400 F. In a large bowl toss eggplant, zucchini, potatoes, onion, tomatoes, garlic, olive oil, parsley, oregano, salt, and pepper until every surface is coated.","Pack into a wide baking dish, alternating or layering the vegetables. Pour water around the edge and cover tightly with foil.","Bake 40 minutes. Uncover, turn vegetables gently, and roast 35 to 45 minutes more until the potatoes are tender and the top is richly browned.","Rest 15 minutes. Serve warm or room temperature with feta, bread, and extra olive oil."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":80,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Briam needs more olive oil than a typical sheet-pan vegetable dish. That olive oil, tomato juice, and slow roast create its silky, almost confit-like texture."},{"title":"Punjabi-Style Chana Masala with Basmati Rice","deck":"Tender chickpeas in a dark, tangy onion-tomato masala with toasted spices and fragrant rice.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN + SOAK   |   COOK 75 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chickpeas"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups dried chickpeas, soaked overnight, or 3 cans drained","name":"dried chickpeas, soaked overnight, or 3 cans drained","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 black tea bag, optional, for color","name":"black tea bag, optional, for color","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon salt","name":"salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Masala"},{"text":"3 tablespoons ghee or neutral oil","name":"ghee or neutral oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon cumin seeds","name":"cumin seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, finely chopped","name":"onion, finely chopped","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 to 2 green chiles, minced","name":"green chiles, minced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 cups crushed tomatoes","name":"crushed tomatoes","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 teaspoons ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon turmeric","name":"turmeric","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon Kashmiri chile powder","name":"Kashmiri chile powder","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 teaspoons chana masala spice blend","name":"chana masala spice blend","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon garam masala","name":"garam masala","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon amchur, or 1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"amchur, or 1 tablespoon lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Cilantro and sliced onion","name":"Cilantro and sliced onion","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Rice"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups basmati rice, rinsed","name":"basmati rice, rinsed","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 1/4 cups water","name":"water","qty":2.25,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon salt","name":"salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"}],"steps":["Cook soaked chickpeas with fresh water, tea bag, and salt until creamy inside, 45 to 60 minutes in a pot or about 20 minutes under pressure. Reserve 2 cups cooking liquid. Skip this step for canned chickpeas.","Heat ghee and bloom cumin seeds. Add onion and cook 12 to 15 minutes until deep golden. Add ginger, garlic, and chile for 1 minute.","Add tomatoes, coriander, cumin, turmeric, chile powder, and chana masala. Cook, stirring, until the mixture darkens and oil appears at the edges, 10 to 12 minutes.","Add chickpeas and 1 1/2 cups cooking liquid. Crush a spoonful against the pan and simmer 20 minutes. Finish with garam masala and amchur or lemon. Adjust salt.","For rice, simmer rinsed basmati with water and salt, covered, 12 minutes. Rest 10 minutes, fluff, and serve with chana, cilantro, and onion."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":75,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"The masala is ready only after the raw tomato smell disappears and the oil separates. That patient bhunao step builds restaurant-level depth."},{"title":"Japanese-Style Miso Eggplant Soba","deck":"Caramelized miso-glazed eggplant over buckwheat noodles with sesame, scallion, and a bright soy dressing.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 28 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Eggplant"},{"text":"4 Japanese eggplants or 2 small globe eggplants, halved","name":"Japanese eggplants or 2 small globe eggplants, halved","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3 tablespoons white or awase miso","name":"white or awase miso","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons mirin","name":"mirin","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon sake or water","name":"sake or water","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon sugar","name":"sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Soba"},{"text":"10 ounces dried soba noodles","name":"dried soba noodles","qty":10.0,"unit":"oz","grams":283.5},{"text":"3 tablespoons soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons rice vinegar","name":"rice vinegar","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon mirin","name":"mirin","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon toasted sesame oil","name":"toasted sesame oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon honey or sugar","name":"honey or sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 cucumber, julienned","name":"cucumber, julienned","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 scallions, thinly sliced","name":"scallions, thinly sliced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon toasted sesame seeds","name":"toasted sesame seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Shichimi togarashi, optional","name":"Shichimi togarashi, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Score eggplant flesh in a crosshatch without cutting through the skin. Brush with oil and roast cut-side down at 425 F for 15 minutes.","Mix miso, mirin, sake, sugar, and ginger. Turn eggplant cut-side up, brush generously with glaze, and roast 8 minutes. Broil 1 to 2 minutes until caramelized, watching closely.","Whisk soy, vinegar, mirin, sesame oil, and honey. Cook soba in abundant unsalted water according to package directions, then rinse thoroughly under cold water and drain well.","Toss soba with dressing, cucumber, and scallion. Top with eggplant, sesame seeds, and shichimi."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":28,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Rinsing soba is not optional; it removes surface starch and restores the clean, springy texture."},{"title":"Ethiopian-Style Red Lentil Misir Wot","deck":"Red lentils simmered with long-cooked onion, berbere, ginger, garlic, and spiced butter.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN   |   COOK 50 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Wot"},{"text":"2 cups red lentils, rinsed until the water runs mostly clear","name":"red lentils, rinsed until the water runs mostly clear","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 large red or yellow onions, very finely chopped","name":"red or yellow onions, very finely chopped","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 tablespoons niter kibbeh or butter plus 1 tablespoon oil","name":"niter kibbeh or butter plus 1 tablespoon oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, grated","name":"garlic cloves, grated","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 to 3 tablespoons berbere spice, to taste","name":"berbere spice, to taste","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons tomato paste","name":"tomato paste","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"5 cups vegetable stock or water, plus more as needed","name":"vegetable stock or water, plus more as needed","qty":5.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground cardamom, optional","name":"ground cardamom, optional","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"Injera, rice, or flatbread","name":"Injera, rice, or flatbread","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Plain yogurt and chopped cilantro, optional","name":"Plain yogurt and chopped cilantro, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cook the onions in a dry heavy pot over medium-low heat for 10 minutes, stirring often, until their moisture evaporates. Add niter kibbeh and continue 10 minutes until soft and golden.","Add garlic, ginger, berbere, and tomato paste. Cook 2 to 3 minutes, stirring constantly, until aromatic and brick red.","Add lentils and stock. Simmer uncovered 25 to 35 minutes, stirring frequently, until the lentils collapse into a thick stew. Add water as needed to prevent scorching.","Season with salt and optional cardamom. Rest 10 minutes before serving with injera or rice."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":50,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Berbere varies dramatically in heat. Start with 2 tablespoons and add more after the lentils have simmered, when the spice level is easier to judge."},{"title":"Vietnamese-Style Mushroom Tofu Pho","deck":"A clear plant-based pho broth layered with charred aromatics, toasted spices, mushrooms, and crisp tofu.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 75 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Broth"},{"text":"1 large onion, halved","name":"onion, halved","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4-inch piece ginger, halved","name":"4-inch piece ginger, halved","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"2 star anise","name":"star anise","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cinnamon stick","name":"cinnamon stick","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon coriander seeds","name":"coriander seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon fennel seeds","name":"fennel seeds","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"4 cloves","name":"","qty":4.0,"unit":"clove"},{"text":"1 piece kombu, about 4 inches","name":"piece kombu, about 4 inches","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"6 dried shiitake mushrooms","name":"dried shiitake mushrooms","qty":6.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"10 cups water","name":"water","qty":10.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon vegetarian mushroom seasoning, optional","name":"vegetarian mushroom seasoning, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon rock sugar or brown sugar","name":"rock sugar or brown sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Salt to taste","name":"Salt to taste","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Bowls"},{"text":"1 block extra-firm tofu, pressed and cubed","name":"extra-firm tofu, pressed and cubed","qty":1.0,"unit":"block"},{"text":"8 ounces fresh mushrooms, sliced","name":"fresh mushrooms, sliced","qty":8.0,"unit":"oz","grams":226.8},{"text":"12 ounces flat rice noodles","name":"flat rice noodles","qty":12.0,"unit":"oz","grams":340.2},{"text":"Scallions, cilantro, Thai basil, bean sprouts, lime, and chiles","name":"Scallions, cilantro, Thai basil, bean sprouts, lime, and chiles","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Char onion and ginger under a broiler until blackened in spots. Toast whole spices for 2 minutes.","Combine charred aromatics, spices, kombu, dried shiitake, and water. Bring almost to a simmer, remove kombu after 20 minutes, and gently simmer the rest 40 minutes. Strain.","Season broth with soy, mushroom seasoning, sugar, and salt. It should be aromatic and slightly assertive. Add fresh mushrooms and simmer 5 minutes.","Pan-sear tofu in a little oil until golden. Prepare rice noodles according to package directions.","Divide noodles and tofu among bowls, ladle over boiling broth and mushrooms, and serve with herbs, sprouts, lime, and chiles."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":75,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Kombu turns slimy and can make broth bitter if boiled hard. Remove it before the broth reaches a full boil."},{"title":"Miso-Glazed Salmon Rice Bowl","deck":"Broiled miso salmon with steamed rice, sesame cucumber, edamame, and quick-pickled vegetables.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN + MARINATE   |   COOK 15 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Salmon"},{"text":"4 salmon fillets, 5 to 6 ounces each","name":"salmon fillets, 5 to 6 ounces each","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 tablespoons white miso","name":"white miso","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons mirin","name":"mirin","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon sake or water","name":"sake or water","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon honey or brown sugar","name":"honey or brown sugar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"Bowls"},{"text":"4 cups cooked short-grain rice","name":"cooked short-grain rice","qty":4.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 English cucumber, thinly sliced","name":"English cucumber, thinly sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon rice vinegar","name":"rice vinegar","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon sesame oil","name":"sesame oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 cup shelled edamame","name":"shelled edamame","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Quick-pickled carrots or radishes","name":"Quick-pickled carrots or radishes","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Scallions and toasted sesame seeds","name":"Scallions and toasted sesame seeds","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Mix miso, mirin, sake, soy, honey, and ginger. Coat the salmon and refrigerate 30 minutes to 4 hours.","Toss cucumber with rice vinegar, sesame oil, and a pinch of salt. Let stand while the salmon cooks.","Wipe excess marinade from the salmon so it does not burn. Broil 6 inches from the heat for 7 to 10 minutes, until caramelized and just opaque in the center.","Build bowls with hot rice, salmon, cucumber, edamame, pickles, scallions, and sesame seeds."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":15,"category":"dinner","chefNote":"Miso and sugar scorch quickly. Remove excess glaze before broiling, then brush on a thin fresh layer during the final minute for shine."},{"title":"Mediterranean Shrimp Tomato Orzo","deck":"Tender orzo simmered with fennel, tomato, wine, herbs, spinach, feta, lemon, and quickly cooked shrimp.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 28 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Orzo"},{"text":"1 1/4 pounds large shrimp, peeled and deveined","name":"large shrimp, peeled and deveined","qty":1.25,"unit":"lb","grams":567.0},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 small fennel bulb or onion, finely diced","name":"fennel bulb or onion, finely diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon red pepper flakes","name":"red pepper flakes","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons tomato paste","name":"tomato paste","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 cup crushed tomatoes","name":"crushed tomatoes","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup dry white wine","name":"dry white wine","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups orzo","name":"orzo","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3 cups shellfish-free fish stock or chicken stock","name":"shellfish-free fish stock or chicken stock","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3 cups baby spinach","name":"baby spinach","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"4 ounces feta, crumbled","name":"feta, crumbled","qty":4.0,"unit":"oz","grams":113.4},{"text":"Zest and juice of 1 lemon","name":"Zest and juice of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/3 cup chopped dill and parsley","name":"chopped dill and parsley","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"}],"steps":["Season shrimp. Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wide pan and sear shrimp 45 to 60 seconds per side, just until the surfaces turn pink. Transfer out; they will finish later.","Add remaining oil and cook fennel 6 minutes. Add garlic, pepper flakes, and tomato paste; cook 1 minute. Deglaze with wine and reduce by half.","Add crushed tomatoes, orzo, and stock. Simmer uncovered 10 to 12 minutes, stirring often, until orzo is al dente and creamy. Add a splash of water if it tightens too soon.","Fold in spinach, shrimp, half the feta, lemon zest and juice, and herbs. Cook 1 to 2 minutes, just until shrimp are opaque. Top with remaining feta."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":28,"category":"dinner","warning":"ALLERGY WARNING  This recipe contains shellfish. Do not prepare or eat it with a shellfish allergy. Substitute 1 1/4 pounds cubed salmon, firm white fish, or chicken; cook until just done in the final step."},{"title":"Greek Slow-Roasted Lamb Shanks with Lemon Potatoes","deck":"Fall-apart lamb shanks braised with lemon, garlic, oregano, wine, and potatoes that drink in the pan juices.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 3 HR 15 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Braise"},{"text":"4 lamb shanks, about 1 pound each","name":"lamb shanks, about 1 pound each","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 teaspoons kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","name":"kosher salt and 1 teaspoon black pepper","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, sliced","name":"onion, sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"8 garlic cloves, lightly crushed","name":"garlic cloves, lightly crushed","qty":8.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon chopped rosemary","name":"chopped rosemary","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Zest and juice of 2 lemons","name":"Zest and juice of lemons","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cup dry white wine","name":"dry white wine","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 bay leaves","name":"bay leaves","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"group":"Potatoes"},{"text":"2 pounds Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in wedges","name":"Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in wedges","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Salt and pepper","name":"Salt and pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Parsley to finish","name":"Parsley to finish","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Heat oven to 325 F. Season shanks and brown in olive oil in a Dutch oven, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Transfer out.","Cook onion 6 minutes. Add garlic, oregano, rosemary, and lemon zest for 30 seconds. Add wine and reduce by one-third. Add stock, lemon juice, bay leaves, and shanks.","Cover and braise 2 hours. Turn shanks, add potatoes tossed with olive oil and seasoning, cover, and cook 45 minutes.","Uncover and raise oven to 425 F. Roast 20 to 30 minutes until potatoes brown and shanks are fork-tender. Rest 15 minutes; skim fat and finish with parsley and fresh lemon."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":0,"category":"treat","chefNote":"The final uncovered roast concentrates the braising liquid and crisps the potatoes. Add fresh lemon at the end to restore brightness lost during the long cook."},{"title":"Moroccan Lamb and Apricot Stew","deck":"Tender lamb with saffron, ginger, cinnamon, apricots, chickpeas, toasted almonds, and fresh herbs.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 2 HR 15 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Stew"},{"text":"2 1/2 pounds lamb shoulder, cut in 1 1/2-inch pieces","name":"lamb shoulder, cut in 1 1/2-inch pieces","qty":2.5,"unit":"lb","grams":1134.0},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"3 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, finely chopped","name":"onion, finely chopped","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 teaspoons ground cumin","name":"ground cumin","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 teaspoons ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":2.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground cinnamon","name":"ground cinnamon","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon turmeric","name":"turmeric","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Pinch of saffron, crumbled into 2 tablespoons warm water","name":"Pinch of saffron, crumbled into 2 tablespoons warm water","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"2 cups chicken or lamb stock","name":"chicken or lamb stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 can (15 ounces) chickpeas, drained","name":"(15 ounces) chickpeas, drained","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":425.2},{"text":"1 cup dried apricots, halved","name":"dried apricots, halved","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon honey","name":"honey","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 preserved lemon rind, rinsed and minced, optional","name":"preserved lemon rind, rinsed and minced, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"group":"Finish"},{"text":"1/2 cup toasted almonds","name":"toasted almonds","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Cilantro and parsley","name":"Cilantro and parsley","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Couscous for serving","name":"Couscous for serving","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Season lamb and brown in batches in olive oil. Transfer out.","Cook onion 8 minutes until golden. Add garlic, ginger, cumin, coriander, cinnamon, and turmeric; cook 1 minute.","Return lamb with saffron water and stock. Cover and simmer gently 75 minutes.","Add chickpeas, apricots, honey, and optional preserved lemon. Simmer uncovered 25 to 35 minutes until lamb is tender and sauce is glossy.","Adjust salt and sweetness. Scatter with almonds and herbs and serve over couscous."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":0,"category":"treat","chefNote":"Add dried fruit late so it softens without disappearing. Preserved lemon is powerful; rinse it and use only the rind."},{"title":"Slow Chicken and Vegetable Stew","deck":"A comforting herb-rich stew with tender chicken thighs, potatoes, carrots, peas, and silky broth.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 25 MIN   |   COOK 75 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Stew"},{"text":"2 1/2 pounds boneless or bone-in chicken thighs","name":"boneless or bone-in chicken thighs","qty":2.5,"unit":"lb","grams":1134.0},{"text":"1 1/2 teaspoons kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":1.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 carrots, cut in chunks","name":"carrots, cut in chunks","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 celery ribs, sliced","name":"celery ribs, sliced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons flour, optional","name":"flour, optional","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 tablespoon tomato paste","name":"tomato paste","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"5 cups chicken stock","name":"chicken stock","qty":5.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 pound Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in chunks","name":"Yukon Gold potatoes, cut in chunks","qty":1.0,"unit":"lb","grams":453.6},{"text":"1 bay leaf","name":"bay leaf","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried thyme","name":"dried thyme","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 sprig rosemary","name":"rosemary","qty":1.0,"unit":"sprig"},{"text":"1 cup frozen peas","name":"frozen peas","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/4 cup chopped parsley","name":"chopped parsley","qty":0.25,"unit":"cup"}],"steps":["Season chicken and brown in olive oil in a Dutch oven. Transfer out.","Cook onion, carrots, and celery 8 minutes. Add garlic, flour, and tomato paste; cook 1 minute.","Gradually stir in stock, scraping the pot. Add potatoes, bay, thyme, rosemary, and chicken. Simmer covered 45 to 55 minutes until chicken and potatoes are tender.","Remove bones and skin if using bone-in chicken; shred meat into large pieces and return it to the pot. Add peas for 3 minutes.","Finish with lemon and parsley. Rest 10 minutes so the broth settles and thickens slightly."],"serves":4,"prepMin":25,"cookMin":75,"category":"treat","chefNote":"Brown the chicken and tomato paste before adding liquid. Those two steps give a simple stew the depth of an all-day pot."},{"title":"Slow Mushroom Bourguignon with Mashed Potatoes","deck":"Meaty mushrooms, red wine, pearl onions, carrots, thyme, and a glossy sauce over buttery potatoes.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 75 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Bourguignon"},{"text":"2 pounds mixed mushrooms, such as cremini, oyster, and portobello","name":"mixed mushrooms, such as cremini, oyster, and portobello","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"3 tablespoons olive oil, divided","name":"olive oil, divided","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt and black pepper","name":"kosher salt and black pepper","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 carrots, cut in thick coins","name":"carrots, cut in thick coins","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons tomato paste","name":"tomato paste","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 tablespoons flour","name":"flour","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"2 cups dry red wine","name":"dry red wine","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups vegetable stock","name":"vegetable stock","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon soy sauce","name":"soy sauce","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon dried thyme or 4 fresh sprigs","name":"dried thyme or 4 fresh sprigs","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"2 bay leaves","name":"bay leaves","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 1/2 cups pearl onions, thawed if frozen","name":"pearl onions, thawed if frozen","qty":1.5,"unit":"cup"},{"group":"Mashed potatoes"},{"text":"2 pounds Yukon Gold potatoes, peeled and cut","name":"Yukon Gold potatoes, peeled and cut","qty":2.0,"unit":"lb","grams":907.2},{"text":"4 tablespoons butter","name":"butter","qty":4.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"3/4 cup warm milk","name":"warm milk","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Salt and white or black pepper","name":"Salt and white or black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Brown mushrooms in batches over high heat with 2 tablespoons oil and salt. Do not crowd; let them take on dark color. Transfer out.","Lower heat and cook diced onion and carrots 8 minutes. Add garlic and tomato paste for 1 minute, then flour for 1 minute.","Whisk in wine and reduce by one-third. Add stock, soy, thyme, bay, pearl onions, and mushrooms. Simmer uncovered 35 to 45 minutes until glossy and concentrated.","Boil potatoes in salted water until tender. Drain well, steam dry 2 minutes, then mash with butter and warm milk. Season generously.","Remove bay leaves and adjust the bourguignon with salt, pepper, or a splash of wine vinegar. Spoon over mashed potatoes."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":75,"category":"treat","chefNote":"Mushrooms only brown when the pan is hot and uncrowded. Batch cooking is not optional if you want a deep, savory sauce rather than gray steamed mushrooms."},{"title":"West African-Style Peanut Sweet Potato Stew","deck":"A warming tomato-peanut stew with ginger, chile, sweet potato, chickpeas, greens, and lime.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 45 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Stew"},{"text":"2 tablespoons neutral oil","name":"neutral oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 large onion, diced","name":"onion, diced","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon grated ginger","name":"grated ginger","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"4 garlic cloves, minced","name":"garlic cloves, minced","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 fresh hot chile, minced, or cayenne to taste","name":"fresh hot chile, minced, or cayenne to taste","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 tablespoons tomato paste","name":"tomato paste","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 can (14 ounces) crushed tomatoes","name":"(14 ounces) crushed tomatoes","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":396.9},{"text":"3/4 cup natural peanut butter","name":"natural peanut butter","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"5 cups vegetable stock","name":"vegetable stock","qty":5.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 large sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed","name":"sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 can (15 ounces) chickpeas, drained, optional","name":"(15 ounces) chickpeas, drained, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":425.2},{"text":"1 bunch collards or kale, sliced","name":"collards or kale, sliced","qty":1.0,"unit":"bunch"},{"text":"1 teaspoon ground coriander","name":"ground coriander","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon smoked paprika","name":"smoked paprika","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 lime","name":"lime","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Salt to taste","name":"Salt to taste","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"Rice or millet","name":"Rice or millet","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Cilantro and chopped roasted peanuts","name":"Cilantro and chopped roasted peanuts","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cook onion in oil over medium heat 8 minutes. Add ginger, garlic, chile, coriander, paprika, and tomato paste; cook 2 minutes.","Add crushed tomatoes and simmer 5 minutes. Whisk peanut butter with 1 cup warm stock until smooth, then add it with remaining stock and sweet potatoes.","Simmer 20 minutes. Add optional chickpeas and greens and cook 10 to 15 minutes more, until sweet potatoes are tender and broth is creamy.","Season with salt and generous lime juice. Serve over rice or millet with cilantro and peanuts."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":45,"category":"treat","chefNote":"This is a vegetarian, West African-inspired groundnut stew. Natural peanut butter gives the cleanest flavor; sweetened commercial peanut butter can make the pot cloying."},{"title":"Provencal-Style Seafood and Tomato Stew","deck":"A shellfish-free fish stew with fennel, tomato, saffron, orange, herbs, and garlicky rouille toast.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 30 MIN   |   COOK 45 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Stew"},{"text":"1 1/2 pounds mixed firm fish, such as cod, halibut, salmon, or sea bass, cut in large pieces","name":"mixed firm fish, such as cod, halibut, salmon, or sea bass, cut in large pieces","qty":1.5,"unit":"lb","grams":680.4},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 fennel bulb, thinly sliced, fronds reserved","name":"fennel bulb, thinly sliced, fronds reserved","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 leek, white and pale green parts sliced and washed","name":"leek, white and pale green parts sliced and washed","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"5 garlic cloves, sliced","name":"garlic cloves, sliced","qty":5.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon fennel seeds, crushed","name":"fennel seeds, crushed","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Pinch of saffron","name":"Pinch of saffron","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"1 strip orange zest","name":"strip orange zest","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 cup dry white wine","name":"dry white wine","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 can (28 ounces) whole tomatoes, crushed","name":"(28 ounces) whole tomatoes, crushed","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":793.8},{"text":"3 cups shellfish-free fish stock","name":"shellfish-free fish stock","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"4 thyme sprigs","name":"thyme sprigs","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 bay leaf","name":"bay leaf","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Parsley and lemon juice","name":"Parsley and lemon juice","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Quick rouille"},{"text":"1/2 cup mayonnaise","name":"mayonnaise","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 small garlic clove, grated","name":"garlic clove, grated","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Pinch of saffron soaked in 1 teaspoon hot water","name":"Pinch of saffron soaked in 1 teaspoon hot water","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Pinch of cayenne","name":"Pinch of cayenne","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"1 teaspoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Toasted country bread","name":"Toasted country bread","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cook fennel and leek in olive oil with a pinch of salt for 10 minutes. Add garlic, fennel seed, saffron, and orange zest; cook 1 minute.","Add wine and reduce by half. Add tomatoes, stock, thyme, and bay. Simmer uncovered 25 minutes, then remove thyme, bay, and orange zest.","Season fish and nestle into the simmering broth. Cover and cook gently 5 to 8 minutes, depending on thickness, until just opaque. Do not stir aggressively.","Mix rouille ingredients and spread on toast. Finish stew with parsley, fennel fronds, and lemon. Serve with rouille toast."],"serves":4,"prepMin":30,"cookMin":45,"category":"treat","warning":"SHELLFISH-SAFE VERSION  Traditional Provencal fish stews may include mussels or other shellfish. This version deliberately uses finfish only. With a shellfish allergy, verify that the fish stock is also shellfish-free."},{"title":"Apple with Cinnamon Pecan Butter","deck":"Fresh apple wedges with warm, silky pecan butter made from deeply toasted nuts.","meta":"SERVES 8 SNACK PORTIONS   |   PREP 10 MIN   |   COOK 10 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Pecan butter"},{"text":"2 cups raw pecans","name":"raw pecans","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground cinnamon","name":"ground cinnamon","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon maple syrup, optional","name":"maple syrup, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract, optional","name":"vanilla extract, optional","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"4 crisp apples, such as Honeycrisp or Granny Smith","name":"crisp apples, such as Honeycrisp or Granny Smith","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Lemon wedge","name":"Lemon wedge","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toast pecans at 350 F for 8 to 10 minutes until fragrant. Cool 5 minutes.","Process the warm pecans in a food processor. They will move from crumbs to clumps to a smooth, flowing butter in 5 to 8 minutes; scrape the bowl as needed.","Blend in cinnamon, salt, and optional maple and vanilla. Transfer to a jar.","Slice apples and rub lightly with lemon to slow browning. Serve each portion with about 2 tablespoons pecan butter."],"serves":8,"prepMin":10,"cookMin":10,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Warm toasted nuts release their oils more readily, so no added oil is usually needed. Keep processing through the crumbly stage."},{"title":"Greek Yogurt with Honey and Walnuts","deck":"A classic, simple Greek combination: cool strained yogurt, floral honey, toasted walnuts, and cinnamon.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 5 MIN   |   COOK 5 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Bowls"},{"text":"2 cups full-fat Greek yogurt","name":"full-fat Greek yogurt","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup walnuts","name":"walnuts","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3 tablespoons honey","name":"honey","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Pinch of ground cinnamon","name":"Pinch of ground cinnamon","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Tiny pinch of flaky salt","name":"Tiny pinch of flaky salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Toast walnuts in a dry skillet over medium-low heat for 4 to 5 minutes. Cool and roughly chop.","Divide yogurt among bowls. Drizzle with honey and top with walnuts, cinnamon, and the smallest pinch of flaky salt."],"serves":4,"prepMin":5,"cookMin":5,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Because there are so few ingredients, quality matters: thick yogurt, fresh walnuts, and a fragrant honey make the snack."},{"title":"Hummus with Vegetables and Warm Pita","deck":"Ultra-smooth lemon-tahini hummus finished with olive oil, paprika, crisp vegetables, and hot pita.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 20 MIN   |   COOK 8 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Hummus"},{"text":"2 cans (15 ounces each) chickpeas, drained, or 3 cups very soft cooked chickpeas","name":"(15 ounces each) chickpeas, drained, or 3 cups very soft cooked chickpeas","qty":2.0,"unit":"can"},{"text":"1/2 cup tahini","name":"tahini","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/3 cup fresh lemon juice","name":"fresh lemon juice","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 garlic clove, crushed","name":"garlic clove, crushed","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground cumin, optional","name":"ground cumin, optional","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/3 to 1/2 cup ice water","name":"to 1/2 cup ice water","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"each"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"Extra-virgin olive oil, paprika or sumac, and parsley","name":"Extra-virgin olive oil, paprika or sumac, and parsley","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Carrots, cucumber, bell pepper, radishes, and warm pita","name":"Carrots, cucumber, bell pepper, radishes, and warm pita","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["For extra-smooth hummus, simmer canned chickpeas in water with 1/2 teaspoon baking soda for 8 minutes, then rinse thoroughly.","Blend tahini, lemon, garlic, and salt for 1 minute. With the machine running, drizzle in ice water until the mixture becomes pale and fluffy.","Add chickpeas and optional cumin. Blend 3 to 5 minutes, scraping as needed, until completely smooth. Add more ice water for a soft, swooping texture.","Spread on a plate, make a well, and finish with olive oil, paprika or sumac, and parsley. Serve with vegetables and warm pita."],"serves":4,"prepMin":20,"cookMin":8,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Whipping tahini with lemon and ice water before adding chickpeas is the key to pale, creamy restaurant-style hummus."},{"title":"Jammy Egg with Tomato and Feta","deck":"Seven-minute eggs with ripe tomato, briny feta, oregano, olive oil, and Aleppo pepper.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 8 MIN   |   COOK 7 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Snack"},{"text":"4 large eggs","name":"eggs","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"2 ripe tomatoes, cut in wedges","name":"ripe tomatoes, cut in wedges","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 ounces feta, crumbled or sliced","name":"feta, crumbled or sliced","qty":3.0,"unit":"oz","grams":85.0},{"text":"2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","name":"extra-virgin olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon dried oregano","name":"dried oregano","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Aleppo pepper or red pepper flakes","name":"Aleppo pepper or red pepper flakes","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Flaky salt and black pepper","name":"Flaky salt and black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Warm bread, optional","name":"Warm bread, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Lower eggs into gently boiling water and cook exactly 7 minutes. Transfer to ice water for 3 minutes, then peel.","Arrange tomatoes and feta on plates. Halve the eggs and add them while still warm.","Drizzle with olive oil and season with oregano, Aleppo pepper, flaky salt, and black pepper. Serve with bread if desired."],"serves":4,"prepMin":8,"cookMin":7,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Starting in boiling water gives more predictable yolks. Seven minutes produces a set white and thick, jammy center."},{"title":"Crispy Roasted Chickpeas with Lemon","deck":"Crunchy oven-roasted chickpeas finished with lemon zest, black pepper, and flaky salt.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 10 MIN   |   COOK 35 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Chickpeas"},{"text":"2 cans (15 ounces each) chickpeas, rinsed and drained","name":"(15 ounces each) chickpeas, rinsed and drained","qty":2.0,"unit":"can"},{"text":"2 tablespoons olive oil","name":"olive oil","qty":2.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon garlic powder","name":"garlic powder","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon ground cumin, optional","name":"ground cumin, optional","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Finely grated zest of 1 lemon","name":"Finely grated zest of lemon","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Freshly ground black pepper","name":"Freshly ground black pepper","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Heat oven to 425 F. Dry the chickpeas extremely well between clean towels; discard loose skins.","Toss with olive oil, salt, garlic powder, and cumin. Roast on a bare sheet pan 30 to 38 minutes, shaking every 10 minutes, until crisp.","Turn off the oven, crack the door, and leave chickpeas inside 10 minutes for extra crunch.","Toss while warm with lemon zest and black pepper. Cool completely before storing uncovered or loosely covered."],"serves":4,"prepMin":10,"cookMin":35,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Add lemon zest after roasting. Lemon juice would soften the crisp shells you just created."},{"title":"Chile-Lime Edamame","deck":"Hot edamame tossed with lime zest, chile, sesame, and flaky salt.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 5 MIN   |   COOK 6 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Edamame"},{"text":"1 pound frozen edamame in pods","name":"frozen edamame in pods","qty":1.0,"unit":"lb","grams":453.6},{"text":"1 teaspoon toasted sesame oil","name":"toasted sesame oil","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Zest and juice of 1 lime","name":"Zest and juice of lime","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon chile flakes, gochugaru, or Tajin-style seasoning","name":"chile flakes, gochugaru, or Tajin-style seasoning","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 teaspoon flaky salt","name":"flaky salt","qty":0.5,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon toasted sesame seeds, optional","name":"toasted sesame seeds, optional","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"}],"steps":["Steam or boil edamame according to package directions, usually 5 to 6 minutes. Drain very well.","While hot, toss with sesame oil, lime zest, half the lime juice, chile, salt, and sesame seeds.","Taste and add more lime juice or chile. Serve warm, squeezing the beans from the pods with your teeth and discarding the pods."],"serves":4,"prepMin":5,"cookMin":6,"category":"snack","chefNote":"Use zest for intense lime aroma without making the pods wet. Add juice gradually so the seasoning still clings."},{"title":"Greek Yogurt Orange and Pistachio Cup","deck":"Creamy yogurt with orange, orange-blossom honey, pistachios, and a hint of cinnamon.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 12 MIN   |   COOK 0 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Cups"},{"text":"3 cups full-fat Greek yogurt","name":"full-fat Greek yogurt","qty":3.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3 oranges","name":"oranges","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 tablespoons honey","name":"honey","qty":3.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon orange blossom water, optional","name":"orange blossom water, optional","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/2 cup roasted unsalted pistachios, chopped","name":"roasted unsalted pistachios, chopped","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Pinch of ground cinnamon","name":"Pinch of ground cinnamon","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"text":"Finely grated orange zest","name":"Finely grated orange zest","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Cut peel and pith from oranges, then slice segments from between the membranes over a bowl to catch the juice.","Stir honey with 1 tablespoon captured orange juice and optional orange blossom water. Use orange blossom sparingly.","Layer yogurt, orange segments, and honey syrup in four glasses. Top with pistachios, cinnamon, and orange zest."],"serves":4,"prepMin":12,"cookMin":0,"category":"dessert","chefNote":"Orange blossom water should perfume, not dominate. Measure it; pouring directly from the bottle can overwhelm the dessert."},{"title":"Lemon Granita with Fresh Berries","deck":"Fluffy shards of intensely lemony ice with lightly sweetened fresh berries.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN + FREEZE   |   COOK 5 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Granita"},{"text":"1 cup water","name":"water","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"3/4 cup sugar","name":"sugar","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon finely grated lemon zest","name":"finely grated lemon zest","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 cup fresh lemon juice","name":"fresh lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 cup cold water","name":"cold water","qty":1.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Pinch of salt","name":"Pinch of salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"Berries"},{"text":"2 cups mixed fresh berries","name":"mixed fresh berries","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 tablespoon sugar or honey","name":"sugar or honey","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"1 teaspoon lemon juice","name":"lemon juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"}],"steps":["Bring 1 cup water, sugar, lemon zest, and salt to a simmer, stirring until dissolved. Cool, then stir in lemon juice and cold water.","Pour into a shallow metal pan and freeze 45 minutes. Scrape the icy edges toward the center with a fork. Repeat every 30 minutes for 3 to 4 hours until fluffy.","Toss berries with sugar and lemon and let stand 10 minutes.","Fluff granita one final time and mound into chilled glasses with berries."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":5,"category":"dessert","chefNote":"A shallow metal pan freezes fastest and creates fine crystals. Regular scraping, not one final scrape, makes granita light instead of solid."},{"title":"Cinnamon-Poached Pear with Yogurt","deck":"Tender pears gently poached with cinnamon, vanilla, citrus, and honey, served with cool yogurt.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 15 MIN   |   COOK 30 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Pears"},{"text":"4 firm Bosc pears, peeled, stems intact","name":"firm Bosc pears, peeled, stems intact","qty":4.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"4 cups water","name":"water","qty":4.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1/2 cup honey or sugar","name":"honey or sugar","qty":0.5,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cinnamon sticks","name":"cinnamon sticks","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 vanilla bean, split, or 1 teaspoon vanilla extract","name":"vanilla bean, split, or 1 teaspoon vanilla extract","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"3 strips orange or lemon peel","name":"strips orange or lemon peel","qty":3.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"Pinch of salt","name":"Pinch of salt","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"},{"group":"To serve"},{"text":"2 cups Greek yogurt","name":"Greek yogurt","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"Toasted sliced almonds or walnuts, optional","name":"Toasted sliced almonds or walnuts, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Combine water, honey, cinnamon, vanilla bean, citrus peel, and salt in a saucepan just large enough to hold the pears. Bring to a simmer.","Add pears and cover the surface with a round of parchment to keep them submerged. Simmer very gently 20 to 30 minutes, turning occasionally, until a knife enters easily.","Remove pears. Boil poaching liquid 8 to 12 minutes until lightly syrupy; add vanilla extract now if using instead of a bean.","Serve pears warm or chilled with yogurt, reduced syrup, and optional nuts."],"serves":4,"prepMin":15,"cookMin":30,"category":"dessert","chefNote":"Keep the liquid below a boil once the pears enter. A hard boil can break the fruit before the center becomes tender."},{"title":"Light Coconut Mango Rice Pudding","deck":"Creamy jasmine rice simmered with light coconut milk, vanilla, lime, and fresh mango.","meta":"SERVES 4   |   PREP 10 MIN   |   COOK 35 MIN","ingredients":[{"group":"Pudding"},{"text":"3/4 cup jasmine rice, rinsed","name":"jasmine rice, rinsed","qty":0.75,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"2 cups water","name":"water","qty":2.0,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 can (13.5 ounces) light coconut milk","name":"(13.5 ounces) light coconut milk","qty":1.0,"unit":"can","grams":382.7},{"text":"1/3 cup sugar or maple syrup","name":"sugar or maple syrup","qty":0.3333333333333333,"unit":"cup"},{"text":"1 teaspoon vanilla extract","name":"vanilla extract","qty":1.0,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"1/4 teaspoon kosher salt","name":"kosher salt","qty":0.25,"unit":"tsp"},{"text":"Finely grated zest of 1 lime","name":"Finely grated zest of lime","qty":1.0,"unit":"each"},{"group":"Finish"},{"text":"2 ripe mangoes, diced","name":"ripe mangoes, diced","qty":2.0,"unit":"each"},{"text":"1 tablespoon lime juice","name":"lime juice","qty":1.0,"unit":"tbsp"},{"text":"Toasted coconut flakes or sesame seeds, optional","name":"Toasted coconut flakes or sesame seeds, optional","qty":null,"unit":"as needed"}],"steps":["Combine rice and water in a saucepan. Bring to a simmer, cover, and cook 12 minutes.","Add coconut milk, sugar, vanilla, and salt. Simmer uncovered over low heat 18 to 22 minutes, stirring often, until creamy but still loose.","Stir in lime zest. Cool 10 minutes; the pudding will thicken as it stands. Thin with a splash of coconut milk if serving chilled.","Toss mango with lime juice. Spoon pudding into bowls and top with mango and optional toasted coconut."],"serves":4,"prepMin":10,"cookMin":35,"category":"dessert","chefNote":"Stop cooking while the pudding still looks slightly loose. Rice continues absorbing liquid as it cools, and overcooked pudding becomes stiff."}];
